{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "purpose": "simulation Phase 1d benchmarks (#841): the plan's section 5 cases, run by CASA's sm and by casa-rs",
  "notes": [
    "Cases run in file order: 5 (write-only, then noise-only), 1, 3, 2, 4.",
    "Case 1 is a 256-plane cube model; case 3 is case 1 with one model plane spanning the band; case 5 is case 1 with observe only.",
    "Case 4 carries July's analytic-model record (docs/tutorial-parity/synthetic-ms-families.md: 1,253 MB/s, a 1 GiB VLA-D Q-band mosaic of 64 channels, 4 correlations and 7 pointings predicted from tools/perf/imager/models/14pt-3gauss-v1.json) as a component list: the model's 14 points and 3 Gaussians with their fluxes, spectral indices (at 43 GHz) and Gaussian axes, offset from 13h +34d by their l and m. Its lines and absorption, which a CASA spectral index cannot express, are left out. Seven pointings 31 arcsec apart (a hexagon about the centre) of 1,780 s each give 437,346 rows. It has no setvp: the VLA's default voltage pattern is #871's.",
    "Each of 'complists' is written by the oracle with CASA's cl tool under its output's complists/, and a predict's complist names one.",
    "Each model is named relative to the oracle's --model-root and is written by make_bench_model.py from the 'models' entry of the same name (casa_sm_predict_oracle.write_model's arguments). Its direction is its case's field centre and its spectral axis is its case's window: a window off the model's band predicts zero.",
    "Cells spread the visibilities over the uv grid: 0.1 arcsec for ALMA cycle10.3 at 230 GHz, 8 arcsec for VLA-D at 1.4 GHz.",
    "Times and configurations keep every case free of shadowing and elevation flags."
  ],
  "models": {
